#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""claude-watch: know when a Claude Code session is waiting on you.

Claude Code fires a `Notification` hook whenever a session stalls on a
permission prompt, an idle prompt, or an MCP dialog. This utility registers
itself on that hook (plus a few lifecycle events), keeps a record of which
sessions are blocked and for how long, and sends a desktop notification (macOS
or Windows), re-notifying while a session stays blocked.

  claude-watch install      register the hooks in ~/.claude/settings.json
  claude-watch status       what is waiting on you right now
  claude-watch log          history of waits, with how long each one took
  claude-watch focus <n>    bring a blocked session's terminal to the front

Run `claude-watch help` for the full list.
"""

